A||||5||Hippocrat||Are Fieros the only car in the world that use these front pads?||||8||
Z||000000||Hippocrat||10-29-2001||01:04 AM||||Stopped at a crappy tire store the other day to pick up some supplies. While I was there I knew I was going to need front pads, so I priced them out at 35 bucks. <P>NOW heres the thing I asked the guy <BR>"Do you have a set in stock" <BR>"Yep"<BR>"Are you sure??"<BR>At this point he is annoyed but answers Yes.<P>I thought about it for a moment but thought Id leave it for another day. Went home and did the stuff I had planned for the day. Finished ahead of schedule so I figure why not do the front brakes? Sent the wife 60 clicks to the same Canadian tire. <P>No pads in stock. He made a mistake. <P>Believe it or not though they had a set of premium pads in stock (what a shock) 70 bucks as opposed to 35 for the standard. Needles to say I bought them from another store (still paid 70 but to a more local store). <P>Anyway. NOBODY stocks these pads. Aren't there any other cars that use these pads. You would think that GM made them specifically for the Fieros. you have to order them in advance if you want them. They have to be used on some other vehicle. <BR>It's not important just annoying.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Philphine||10-29-2001||08:59 AM||||what year is it? i know when they first came out they used modded chevette front suspension pieces. don't know about brakes but if you have access to an interchange manual (i've looked at one in the local library before) you might find out for sure.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-29-2001||12:08 PM||||I've not had any problem finding them....<P>You can't expect parts stores to stock every part for every old car... Most can get whatever part within 24-48 hours. Sometimes the same day depending on the store.<P>They usually only have room onsite for stuff they know thay can move in volume. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-29-2001||12:10 PM||||I havent found anything that would fit so far,  I think I will upgrade my front to the grandam brakes also (switched my back ones awhile back)<P>PS..Can.Tire has the "premium" here also but no whitebox ones  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||dcaprio||10-30-2001||07:28 AM||||My local auto stores all had them in stock , front and rear. They had several different grades of pads. I called around and got the best price. ||||reg||1
